{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-008", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India, MERCOSUR move towards wider preferential trade pact", "content": "India and MERCOSUR have launched negotiations to expand their existing Preferential Trade Agreement and are finalising terms of reference for the wider pact. \nA new protocol gives electronic Certificates of Origin the same legal value as paper documents. \nThe changes aim to cut transaction costs, speed origin checks and improve preferential trade. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-mercosur-move-towards-wider-preferential-trade-pact-313471-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-009", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh allows no-limit imports without LCs under new policy", "content": "Bangladesh Bank has guided authorised dealer banks on the 2026-2029 Import Policy Order, allowing permissible industrial and commercial imports by contract without LCs. \nThe change can widen payment options for apparel and textile sourcing, subject to foreign exchange compliance. \nExport-oriented factories may procure local inputs through back-to-back LCs or free-of-cost arrangements. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-allows-no-limit-imports-without-lcs-under-new-policy-313469-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-010", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["order_visibility"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Can PTA stay firm as crude rises and polyester demand sags?", "content": "PTA markets are firmer this week as a sharp crude oil rally lifts feedstock costs, despite subdued polyester and textile demand ahead of the traditional peak season.\nSpot PTA and paraxylene values across Asian and Western hubs edged higher over September 7-11, 2026.\nChina maintenance restarts are lifting operating rates and easing spot availability, while weak order intake may cap further gains.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/can-pta-stay-firm-as-crude-rises-and-polyester-demand-sags--313467-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-011", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "India-UK CETA: The door is open, but is everyone ready?", "content": "India-UK CETA has opened new opportunities for Indian exporters, with buyer enquiries already beginning to come in. \nPunjab MSMEs, including Ludhiana’s woollen knitwear and hosiery cluster, are still grappling with compliance details. \nExporters need rules-of-origin knowledge, stronger records and documentation, plus workshops and sector-specific handholding. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-uk-ceta-the-door-is-open-but-is-everyone-ready--313465-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-012", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Global apparel trade 2026: Who wins the $550 bn share war?", "content": "China, Bangladesh and Vietnam dominate the $546.8 billion garment market, with 2026 sourcing flows splintering across more countries.\nUS apparel imports fell 8.65 per cent in January-July 2026; Vietnam led; Bangladesh stayed ahead of China and Cambodia rose 10.48 per cent.\nBuyers are using more sourcing markets but consolidating around suppliers with flexibility, traceability and compliance.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/global-apparel-trade-2026-who-wins-the-550-bn-share-war--313476-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-013", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Can Indian apparel exporters beat the rising cost crunch?", "content": "Cotton yarn prices in India have risen from about ₹250 a kg in early 2026 to around ₹400, pressuring apparel exporters’ fabric and garment costs.\nAEPC has urged government action to regulate cotton-yarn exports of 20s count and above as flows to Bangladesh and Vietnam increase.\nTiruppur estimates production costs are up 15 per cent; raw cotton duty relief may be extended beyond October 31.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/can-indian-apparel-exporters-beat-the-rising-cost-crunch--313454-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-15-014", "date": "2026-09-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India's apparel retail revenue to grow 12-13% in FY27: Crisil Ratings", "content": "Crisil Ratings projects 12-13 per cent revenue growth for organised apparel retail in India this fiscal, down from about 15 per cent last year.\nValue fashion and tier-II, tier-III expansion are driving volumes, but rising cotton and operating costs may pull margins to 14 per cent.\nFestive demand, store productivity and responsive sourcing will shape full-year performance and supplier planning.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-apparel-retail-revenue-to-grow-12-13-in-fy27-crisil-ratings-313449-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
